- `cbor_bytestring_handle(hash_item_value)` returns `(unsigned char *)v`
- `cbor_bytestring_length(hash_item_value)` reads 8 bytes from offset 8 of the union

For a uint item, offset 8 of the union would be whatever follows the uint value. In the cbor_item_t struct, after the union, there are `type`, `refcount`, etc. But offset 8 is still within the union (the union is at least 16 bytes for bytestring). So offset 8 would be uninitialized or part of the next field.

